    "title": "When does Ramadan end? Eid to come on Friday",
    "text": "MICHIGANIs Eid Thursday? Here's when Muslim holiday beginsJenna Prestininzi Mariyam MuhammadUSA TODAY NETWORKMarch 18, 2026Updated March 19, 2026, 7:07 a.m. ETSubscribe to hear this storyThe wait is almost over for Muslim communities across Michigan, Eid celebrations will get underway on Friday, March 20.Eid al-Fitr has been confirmed for Friday, March 20, according to Saudi Arabian moon spotters. The holiday's date depends on the crescent moon sighting according to the Islamic lunar calendar, and was expected for either Thursday, March 19 or Friday, March 20.",
